On Tue, 8 Feb 2005, Manuel wrote:
[...]
> My questions are:
> 1) Should I *always* be much more careful when kicking doors open?

Probably only in Minetown. The guards there will get angry if you try
to pick a lock in plain sight, do something with the fountains (in
plain sight) or destroy doors in plain sight. (If no one sees it, you
won't get into trouble... I *think*. It's best just to get a skeleton
key or cast knock to open doors in Minetown.) For the rest of the
dungeon, door-kicking is relatively safe, although there's a small
chance it will be booby-trapped, in which case you might get stunned.


> 2) Should I have defended myself and killed the guards? What would have
> happened then?

You'd just have to sacrifice monsters to mollify your deity. You may
also lose telepathy if you kill the guards, though.


> 3) What can I get from the priest in the minetown temple? I he always
> co-aligned?
[...]

He's not always co-aligned. But regardless of that, all priests can
give you protection. (Google for the "donating to priests" spoiler for
more info.) But it's a matter of knowing how much to give. It's not as
simple as simply giving everything you got.


